  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 250 PM EST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\n- Quiet weather through the remainder of the work week\n\nQuiet weather is expected through the work week. Ridging will\nbuild aloft into Wednesday, before a shortwave trough topping the\nridge flattens it some as we head into Thursday. Prior model runs\nhad some light rain in the Thursday and Thursday night time \nframe, but that has changed and we now look dry. A weak surface \ncold front will pass through on Thursday with little fanfare. The \nupper shortwave looks to pass well off to our north. Given the\nabove factors, dry weather is expected through Friday. In fact, all\nGFS and ECMWF ensemble members are dry through Friday. \n\nWe move into deep southwest flow on Tuesday and that remains in\nplace all the way through Saturday. A gradual warming trend will\nbe the result. High temperatures this week will steadily warm each\nday through the 50s. By Friday and Saturday 60s are anticipated. \n\n- Chances for rain this weekend\n\nAs we head into the weekend a shortwave trough will swing east\nfrom the Northern Plains into the Great Lakes. The wave will\neliminate the ridge and replace it with zonal flow. A surface cold\nfront is forecast to sweep through the area Saturday night which\nis when we will carry the highest chances for precipitation (60-80\npercent). Temperatures will cool as we head into Sunday and next \nMonday. 850mb temperatures will peak near +10C this week, falling\ninto the zero to -5C range on Monday. Highs next Monday look to \nfall back to near 40. For perspective, the normal high at Grand\nRapids today is 47.\n\nOverall, a very quiet weather week by November standards.",
